ever commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Run your own package tests and the harnesses BEFORE handoff, then the full configured suite once (read the command count from the candidate config). Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-32ypr2 --role developer` so revision 4 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in.\n9|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt died mid-way, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n10|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 4.","final_result":true}}}
