{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c545","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b48a-1840-7d93-9d43-f2decee529f8"},"sequence":253,"recorded_at":1780531400000501,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15"},"call_id":"call_01a0b48affa17037b7af8b54466f8bac","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/base-refresh/replay-256112823/worktree/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-18\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-2056mm rev3 — Binding-parser rework: closed-shape arms, identity pre-transform walk, stated bounds\n9|- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (no P1; P2-1 production at the Binding parser, five P3; the reviewer reproduced the v4 payloads, evidence/identity/recovery/authority behavior, the registry re-pin, and the harness 30/30 twice — all kept). P2-1: `ParseTerminalBinding` now enforces `protocol_version` major 1 (`isProtocolMajorOne` over the landed semver grammar, verdict-agreed with `CheckVersionTuple` on a 14-version corpus) and `extensions == {}` (landed strict frame, zero members) per the §4.B table, and `bindingIdentity` refuses JSON numbers at any depth plus nested duplicate members before the JCS transform (strict UseNumber decode with per-depth dup refusal, mirroring the landed terminalbackend decode+walk — digest-equality and verdict agreement pinned, including a numeric extension value). Every member arm of the table is now driven negatively through the entry (37-subtest battery with code+detail pins) with six new narrowing rows (major, extensions, number, nested-dup, supersedes, pre-read generation bound). P3-2: `EmitResumed` checkpoint/pair binding stated explicitly as a caller bound with a boundary-pinning test (fabricated checkpoint appends; fold reports it newest). P3-3: generation-bound-before-read witness committed with its row. P3-4: pre-scan harness notes corrected to the documented redundancy, README bootstrap sentence corrected to the plain refusal, `resolve.go` \"every failure\" scoped to resolution failures, row 57 / 5.2#18 restated as a bound, descriptor test added to the identity-exact case. P3-5: restore/terminate-stale execution deferred to a Story follow-up task (no board task exists yet — no brief assigned it); the kkh1an `HandoffFailed` note is NOT APPLICABLE (this leaf wires no reporter).\n10|- CORRECTION to the rev1 entry's F2 (appended, history preserved): \"the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals)\" is wrong for the two body surfaces — the landed `ParseMutationContext`/`ParseStatusBody` refuse a forbidden identity with the SAME pinned `terminal_backend_protocol_error`; the pre-scans add only the Go error type (`*terminalbackend.Error`), and no wrapper exists for the bootstrap surface at all (landed `Store.Bind` refuses plain and uncoded). The wrappers stay as a documented redundancy with corrected notes.\n11|- F1: a major-1 selection over an already-validated semver needs no integer parse — the major is the digit run before the first dot, so prefix `1.` is exact with no saturation class for huge foreign majors; the 14-version agreement battery against `CheckVersionTuple` (grammar faults, majors 0/2/3/10, a 2^64-scale major, prerelease/build spellings) proves no second model.\n12|- F2: `bindingIdentity`'s old \"no number can reach the digest by check ordering\" comment was false exactly where extension values are untyped — the pre-transform walk must be structural (decode + walk), not an ordering claim; the direct-identity hostile battery (numbers, nested dups, trailing data, depth/size caps) pins the walk independently of the member arms that now fire first.\n13|- AC: 65 of 66 rows driven through production entries by named tests (row 57 restated as a bound — no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk; rows 61–66 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`). MUTATION EVIDENCE: 34 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary arm-delete row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. Registry: 5.2 gap reworded to the row-57 bound, eight test citations added across four cases with mirror updates, digest re-derived `b09b5b9f…` (canonical bytes 167094), tracecheck green `63/574` with identical section ratios. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n14|\n15|### TASK-260830-2056mm rev2 — Race-gate rework: per-subtest evidence universes\n16|- REWORKED after the rev1 CR validation stopped at command 5/30 (`go test ./... -race`): one DATA RACE in `TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe` — four parallel subtests shared a single `mapUniverse` while the two \"second\" cases extended it, racing the sibling `Lookup` reads (`resolve_test.go:172/181` vs `fixtures_test.go:490`). The race detector then failed the whole `termbind` package; every other package was green. Fix is test-only: each subtest builds its own `universeMap(t, world)` copy (rev2 delta vs the rev1 candidate is exactly this hunk, proven by whole-tree diff of the reconstructed rev1 tree). No production byte changed; the `N-resolve-manifest-count` killer still kills its narrowing mutant.\n17|- VERIFIED: `go test ./internal/termbind/ -race -count=10` green (plus two more `-count=3` passes), siblings `axpane`/`terminstance` `-race` green, `mutant_harness.py` 30/30 on two identical passes, gofmt/vet/build clean, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical, trunk still `c3aae73` (no refresh). Full 30-command suite reruns automatically at handoff.\n18|- F1: a shared mutable map across `t.Parallel()` subtests fails the entire package under `-race`, not just the racing test — every concurrently running test reports \"race detected during execution of test\", so one fixture race reads as fifteen failures. Fixture isolation per subtest is the fix; read-only sharing (as in `TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds`) stays safe.\n19|\n20|### TASK-260830-2056mm — Terminal binding events and recovery (story-final leaf)\n21|- DELIVERED: `internal/termbind` — the §4.1/4.B-4.D/5.2-Terminal-Events/7.A final leaf over the landed owners and the story's own `axpane`/`terminstance`: `ParseTerminalBinding` owns the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object no parser existed for (ID recomputed before use, construction byte-agreed with the landed manifest admission); `CheckInstanceIdentity` + the operation-body pre-scans refuse the eight forbidden identity forms with the pinned protocol class on the Binding, descriptor (adopted landed entry), operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach receipts, with the CLI Result 4 surface a tripwire-pinned bound; `ResolveEvidence` resolves each v4 event's evidence IDs to exactly one Manifest, one Probe, and the Capability Evidence objects bound to the event tuple through the landed `Registry.AdmitProbe` (eleven foreign resolution targets refuse, substitution fails closed); `EmitTerminalCreated`/`EmitResumed` author the v4 payloads under a locally held lease with the digest as the opaque reference; `RecoverCreate` is read-only (absence / ONE child / unavailable+status_first, window from the fold newest); the attach receipt store records one durable receipt per client pair and emits neither event. Takeover selects an admitted backend with a new digest and event, append-only, never a fork; v1 readers stay inert.\n22|- F1: the producer's \"§13.1\" recovery rule lives at §4.1 lines 1395/1399 in the pinned v0.7.0 document (\"status plus that binding MUST