Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\n63|- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\n64|- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n65|\n66|<<<<<<< HEAD\n67|### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev4 — ax pane rework: fold-only newest, resumed-checkpoint closure, replay signal\n68|- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev3 (1 P1 class at two sites, 1 P2, 8 P3): the strict lease/fold equality is deleted — the fold is the sole newest authority and a successor lease's checkpoint is the handoff base at takeover time that never moves, so the only asserted fact is the implication \"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\" at one site directly after fencing (launch and restore alike, parked `restore_policy` on a null fold); `Run` derives the profile closure from the checkpoint actually resumed (required checkpoint, else fold newest, else session head), never `Winner.Checkpoint`; `Supersede` reports the commit-race replay and `Run` flips the post-window loser to `reattach`; the window never closes on the lease record, an unfoldable chain fails the run, and the identity record binds its own `session_id`.\n69|- F1: an immutable handoff base can only ever imply, never equal, a moving newest — the equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint, and relaxing it alone turned the park into a wrong-profile launch, so both sites landed together with the post-takeover lifecycle positive (restore launches with C1's closure) and the wrong-profile plants in both directions through `Run`.\n70|- F2: a store-level replay without a signal is a lie at the call site — `Supersede` replayed the winner's receipt but `Run` reported `launch` with a child it did not create; the `(Binding, bool, error)` signal mirrors `Bind`'s `reattached` and flips the outcome, pinned through `Run` with the `AfterStage` hook.\n71|- F3: per-object classification cannot be derived from an aggregate error — `Reconcile` liveness shares the generic mismatch code and carries no per-row identity, so the `realmRowUsable` copy is a stated classification-only bound, fail-closed both directions; likewise the handoff-base-to-published binding is the takeover leaf's stated obligation.\n72|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 52 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 53/53 with control), including the null-fold conditional row, the closure-source row (a mutant reading `Winner.Checkpoint` again dies), the replay-keeps-launch row, the lease-closes-window row, and the fold-error-laundered row. AC 43/43 re-derived by counting with every named test verified present; the four rev3-unfaithful rows now pin the post-takeover launch positives.\n73|- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n74|\n75|### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev3 — ax pane rework: fold newest, per-pair receipts, credential conditional\n76|- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev2 (1 P1 class, 2 P2, 8 P3): the bootstrap window, checkpoint admission, and journal source binding now read the chain fold's newest checkpoint (`sessstate.Reduce` → `Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest.ID`) instead of the lease record's checkpoint, which is null for every epoch-1 owner; a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold; superseded pairs keep per-operation receipts (`receipts/<op>.json`, no-replace per pair) with the first binding as the in-window anchor; `Run` fails when a checkpoint-carrying winner has no checkpoint store bound; the §4.C credential conditional applies to every caller with `Smoke.Required`, the realm cross-bind accepts any binding object, and dead (expired/pre-reboot) realm evidence refuses the typed `capability_unavailable`.\n77|- F1: lease records are immutable content-addressed blobs — `CreateLease` mints epoch-1 with a null checkpoint and only a takeover mints a checkpoint-carrying successor — so \"the winning lease's checkpoint\" can never be the newest-checkpoint authority; the ordinary same-host story (stopped with C on epoch 1) is the test that catches the confusion at all three gates (window/admission/journal) at both `Decide` and `Run`.\n78|- F2: per-pair receipts keep the §4.1 replay contract (\"identical retry replays it\", keyed `session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id`) while the first-binding anchor keeps the in-window mutual exclusion the link race proved; `SessionBound` scans anchor-or-receipts so a crash between installs cannot reopen the window.\n79|- F3: `Reconcile` fails before the realm arm runs, so dead realm evidence needs a refusal mapping, not a wider gate: the mapping fires only when the caller needs the realm row, submitted a realm row, and none is usable — a usable row plus an unrelated backend fault keeps the backend class.\n80|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 47 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 48/48 with control), including one narrowing mutant per P1-1 conditional (window-fold, null-fold ×2, newest, agreement ×2) and the RV7 losing-epoch row the rev2 suite survived. AC 43/43 re-derived by counting (rev2's \"41 of 41\" restated a 43-row denominator; the reviewer measured 39/43).\n81|- REVERSAL (P1-1, stated explicitly): this entry's \"a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold\" is FALSE as of rev4 — a successor lease's `checkpoint_id` is the handoff base at takeover time and never moves, while every checkpoint the successor owner publishes afterwards lands on the chain, so the strict equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint and parked every session that was ever taken over. The fold is the sole newest authority; the only asserted fact is the implication \"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\" (one site, directly after fencing), and the profile closure comes from the checkpoint actually resumed, never `Winner.Checkpoint`.\n82|- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n83|=======\n84|### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\n85|\n86|- DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\n87|- ORDERING (the task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests (pre and post) — the gate proved them equal before the seal ran, so the sealed bytes equal either measurement — and the ordering mutants prove the gate precedes the seal at both entries: `N-race-order-capture` (manifest scan), `N-race-order-project` (seal error message), `N-race-order-project-seal` (capture-store scan at the projection entry). Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file, excluded size change, and unreadable-at-post each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\n88|- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, every-payload-blob-installed assertion after Capture and after the crash replay, target-sink-empty assertion on the archive path, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 41 narrowing + 2 add-write rows KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry and the cross-package P3-ε row (plant in clonebundle, killer here). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n89|- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260918-fdce92; no base move, still `2f844bb` over trunk `a12d1bd`; `origin/main` still `c3aae73`): row 8 sealed unstable pre/post digests + generation asserted against the measurements (`N-unstable-seals-pre-as-post`); row 10 capture-store manifest scan at `CaptureAndProject` (`N-race-order-project-seal`, killed by the scan — `N-race-order-project` is killed by the seal error message); P3-a unplanned-symlink row, P3-b symlinked-store-root row, P3-c excluded-size row (shipped, not reworded); P3-d branch bound attributed to the landed `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` with a first-hand survival probe; P3-e four rows shipped (plan grammar, required blockedAncestor, fingerprints-129, first-chunk-oversize). Only production edit is the ORDER-PIN comment (inert receipt clause fixed).\n90|- INHERITED (rev2 rework): P3-ε CLOSED here (excluded unknown drives `raw_complete=false` and blocks `maximal_safe` at this leaf's projection entry, test + cross-package harness row); P3-ζ DEFERRED to TASK-260830-32ypr2 (no title/text admission site in this leaf); P3-η PARTIAL — this leaf's entry re-validation pinned by test, the standalone `EncodeNativeIdentity` contract deferred to the clonebundle owner or the final leaf. P3-γ sealed the measured post digest; P3-δ reworded as defence-in-depth; P3-ε′ orphan-blob row shipped; P3-ζ′ fidelity duplication recorded as a bound.\n91|- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): no `ax` CLI/provider process/network (fixture store); Section 7.8 operation wiring stays `sessadapter`; projection planning past admission is the final leaf's; excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor (never opened by design); sub-walk transient swaps restored before post-measure are below the floor (no fs snapshot). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n92|- AC: 17 of 17 rows driven through production entries by named tests and measured at the member level — every row's narrowing reddens its killer (matrix in `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`).\n93|>>>>>>> 3005d78 (TASK-260830-2g5be6: TASK-260830-2g5be6: implement-native-capture-and-source-race-check)\n94|\n95|## 2026-09-17\n96|\n97|### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev2 — ax pane rework: authority, window, closure, realm\n98|- REWORKED on `888ae3d` after review-verdict-rev1 (18 findings): event authority through `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` with local-hold-only emission and the §5.7 fold gate (`sessstate.Reduce`); realm authorization through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to host binding/build/generation (bare boolean removed); bootstrap window closed by the winner's `HasCheckpoint` with atomic `Supersede`; checkpoint admission bound to the winning lease and session; profile from the checkpoint closure (`DeriveForHeads`); journal source bound to the lease checkpoint; non-interactive `headless_creation` conditional; remote non-interactive parks per §4.2 step 5.\n99|- F1: a park decision's stale/unverified presented token never authors — `Emit` presents the winning tuple itself, so verified local-winner parks (stale, material, checkpoint) emit while remote/unverified/ambiguous/handoff parks refuse; `Run` pre-checks local hold + foldability and parks without evidence rather than manufacturing a §5.2 collision.\n100|- REVERSAL (P3-8, stated explicitly): rev1 F1's \"both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`\" is FALSE as of rev2 — `attach_remote`, `takeover_offer`, and every remote park author no chain event, because the local wrapper cannot append under another host's lease (§5.2: the winning owner serializes state-changing events); the decision itself is the parked evidence.\n101|- F2: the bootstrap window is the winner's `HasCheckpoint`, not a clock: in-window changed ops refuse `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes, post-window new ops supersede via staged rename; the `binding-*.tmp` sweep is age-gated (1 min) so a concurrent live stage is never deleted.\n102|- F3: resume profile is the checkpoint closure, not the head: `Run` loads the winner's heads even when the checkpoint is not otherwise required, so a head-only or losing-lease `profile.changed` never drives launch (§2.4, §13.10).\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
