ernal/crashgate) conformance harness, whose\n3444|undischarged clauses `13.13#4` and `13.13#5` are the rollback/parked\n3445|visibility sentences through event, CLI/status, audit, and\n3446|lifecycle-projection surfaces this repository has no binary or projection to\n3447|produce; Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n3448|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n3449|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; Section\n3450|5.3 at 7/8, bound to\n3451|[`internal/sessrepo`](internal/sessrepo), whose undischarged clause `5.3#5`\n3452|is the initiator-union maximum no takeover flow computes yet; Section\n3453|15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n3454|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n3455|the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n3456|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n3457|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no\n3458|provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a TerminalBackend\n3459|capability. Structural RPC hello frames are built by\n3460|[`internal/rpcwire`](internal/rpcwire), which rejects an error map key, and\n3461|consumed by the authenticated [`internal/hostchannel`](internal/hostchannel)\n3462|handshake, which frames failures only as Error envelopes and never as hello\n3463|keys; neither clause is enumerated against an acceptance case, so both stay\n3464|undischarged. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\n3465|[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\n3466|an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\n3467|carries no Structured Error code, so the prohibition holds and the clause\n3468|stays undischarged. The same package carries the Section 4 lifecycle,\n3469|attach, entrypoint, replication, and historical-translation conformance\n3470|harness (`conformance.go`, exercised by `conformance_test.go`) and an\n3471|AST-derived refusal-arm inventory (`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`) that\n3472|requires every production refusal arm to be declared with a resolving named\n3473|asserting test in both directions; behavioral proof stays with each row's\n3474|named test, which the inventory resolves textually; and Section 7.7 at 3/4,\n3475|bound to [`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost), whose undischarged clause\n3476|`7.7#2` is the machine-local-alias sentence - the omit rule is enforced, but a\n3477|shell word that expands to unrestricted mode without spelling a table token is\n3478|beyond argv inspection; Section 11.2 at 3/5, bound to\n3479|[`internal/rpcwire`](internal/rpcwire), whose undischarged clauses `11.2#1`\n3480|and `11.2#5` are the hello-first sequencing sentences - the stateless codec\n3481|has no handshake memory and no legacy responder exists, so only the\n3482|RPC-5 Host Channel lane executes them; and Section 17.1 at 3/6, bound to\n3483|[`internal/meshneg`](internal/meshneg), whose undischarged clauses `17.1#2`,\n3484|`17.1#3`, and `17.1#6` are minor-version preservation, immutable-object\n3485|extensions, and v1 materialization upgrade, none of which a major-only\n3486|negotiator implements; and Section 7.A at 1/2, bound to\n3487|[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend), whose discharged\n3488|descriptor-rejection clause is enforced by `AdmitProviderDescriptor` while\n3489|the LeaseToken v2 fencing rule stays with the provhost v2 machinery),\n3490|nine are\n3491|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n3492|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n3493|implementation; Section 5.5 at 1/3, whose discharged negative-battery clause\n3494|is enforced by identity creation and checking while the opaque-map content\n3495|rule stays half-decided; Section 8 at 4/12, whose discharged probe,\n3496|label-integrity, and row-separation clauses are enforced by the resume tuple\n3497|gate and the native-resume smoke while every materialization rule stays\n3498|unimplemented; and Section 2.2 at 4/22, bound to\n3499|[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing), whose discharged clauses are the\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
