{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d269","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b48a-1840-7d93-9d43-f2decee529f8"},"sequence":1935,"recorded_at":1780531400003865,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b494-2be6-7da3-8461-c34c852f32a5"},"task_id":"01a0b494-2be6-7da3-8461-c34c852f32a5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b494-2be6-7da3-8461-c34c852f32a5","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-32ypr2 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 3\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-d009f2 (claude-opus-5 max, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-32ypr2-3` revision 3 (story_final), base\n5|`c3aae73df906df1b5aa962c7bc3c16437dd920fa` (= `origin/main`, re-fetched at\n6|review start, unmoved), candidate tree\n7|`fc597b8415e4b1440aa2bc12560fdf8f5b668311` (66 paths; patch sha256\n8|`06ace981df5e81452b2857ddf0f47436729a7e0a58d2cb9e54b59fdeda3302e8`, verified\n9|against the attached resource). The live Story worktree's temp-index tree\n10|OID (`git add -A` into a scratch index) equalled `fc597b84…` before this\n11|review; `git status` stayed ` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`,\n12|` M internal/clonesnap/{TRACEABILITY.md,project.go}`,\n13|` M internal/traceability/{6 files}`, `?? internal/cloneproject/` throughout.\n14|Worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched. Authority:\n15|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (10331–10546), §10.2, §7.8.\n16|\n17|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree\n18|(`git archive fc597b84…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-32ypr2/review-rev3/{candidate,\n19|probe,battery,plant}`; the tracked `.task-board` dropped from the copies and\n20|re-materialized only for the `specpin` board-scope test); `diff -rq` clean\n21|between `candidate` and `battery`/`plant` after every harness and plant run;\n22|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` on every harness, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` after\n23|the runs. Every probe named below was executed on the candidate copy; logs,\n24|per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits, and the probe sources are in\n25|`TASK-260830-32ypr2_review-evidence-rev3.tar.gz`.\n26|\n27|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n28|\n29|No P1. One P2 (new, outside the rev2 rework scope) and a P3 list. The rev2\n30|rework is CLOSED AT THE CLASS, not only at the witnessed vectors — Section 0\n31|below is unqualified. What remains is one AC-named invariant that the\n32|committed suite measures only in its degenerate case: raw-reference\n33|byte ranges resolve to the captured bytes for single-record members\n34|(offset 0) and are never witnessed at a non-zero offset, so the natural\n35|one-token bug in the offset accumulation survives the whole suite while\n36|matrix row 4 reports the property as driven. Production is correct (probed);\n37|the rework is test-plus-matrix only and small.\n38|\n39|## Section 0 — rev2 rework verification (RUN-260918-a4ffef findings)\n40|\n41|| Finding | Grade | Evidence |\n42||---|---|---|\n43|| P1-b second lenient decoder after the strict gate | CLOSED AT THE CLASS | `grep -n 'NewDecoder\\|Unmarshal' internal/cloneproject/*.go` (non-test): the only decodes are `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (`native.go:77`), five `json.Unmarshal(members[field.name], *string)` reads by exact name (`native.go:125`), `Body = members[\"body\"]` (`:135`), `CheckUint53Bounds(members[\"v\"], 1, 1)` (`:136`), body-member reads from the strict body map (`:293`, `:307`, `:390`) and the sealed-manifest map read by exact key (`normalize.go:222`). No struct decode of the line remains. Re-driven on the pristine candidate through `clonesnap.Capture` → `Normalize` (`logs/probe-section0.log`): PA1/PA2 → `opaque_event`, evidence `native_type=\"frobnicate\"` in both document orders; PA3 → `Instruction.Found=false`, payload `authority=low`; PA4 → content `declared`; PA5 → evidence `evt-a5`; PA6 → refused `body carries unknown member \"text\"`; PA7 → refused `subagent:ghost ... no mapped UUID`; PA8 control admitted. Class, not spelling: every claimed member aliased at once with other spellings (`V`, `NATIVE_EVENT_ID`, `Native_Type`, `ORIGIN`, `PROTECTION`, `ACTOR`, `BODY`) → `opaque_event frobnicate evt-c1`; `\"v\":1,\"V\":2` admitted, `\"v\":2,\"V\":1` refused; body-level aliases (`TEXT`, `Authority`) refuse as unknown members; an escaped-key duplicate (`\"native\\u005ftype\"` beside `\"native_type\"`) refuses `duplicate member`; a mapped `subagent:ghost` with an `Actor` alias attributes to the subagent UUID. |\n44|| the case-folded narrowing DIES | CONFIRMED, and the CLASS mutants die too | Producer rows `N-alias-{native-type,origin,protection,body,native-event-id,actor}` KILLED 2/2 (`mutants/producer-run{1,2}/`). My own class plants, run twice against `-run TestNormalize` (`reviewer-plants/run{1,2}/`): `RV-class-struct-redecode` (the rev2 P1-b shape restored: `json.Unmarshal(raw, &envelope)` after the strict map) KILLED, 6 alias subtests fail; `RV-class-equalfold-lookup` (`strings.EqualFold` lookup over the strict map for every claimed string member, order-independent) KILLED, 6 subtests; `RV-class-equalfold-body` (body only) KILLED by `body_alias`. |\n45|| five prose sites | CORRECTED | `native.go:52-57,66-76,104-110` now state the strict-map mechanism; `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md:34` (\"then read from the admitted map by exact member name with no second decoder\"), `:65` (kind aliases in either order stay `opaque_event`), `:102` (envelope values from the strict map; `body_alias`/`evidence_alias`); README:2459-2462 (exact-name sentence, no capability claim); LOGBOOK \"REV3 CORRECTION\" line names the REV2 sentence false with the mechanism (history kept, 36 added / 0 deleted lines vs trunk); results finding table row 1. |\n46|| P2-d `reasoning_summary` positive row | CLOSED | `TestNormalizeReasoningSummaryProjectsInternal` (kind, `internal`, text block, `exact`); `N-reasoning-summary-routed` KILLED 2/2. |\n47|| P3-m..t | CLOSED | `TestNormalizeCaptureStatusExactForEveryKind` + `N-capture-status-partial`; `TestNormalizeLastNativeInstructionWins` + `N-instruction-fold-first`; `TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` + `N-external-actor-kind`; `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unknown_type_without_body` + `N-required-member-body`; `TestNormalizeNullTextDecodesAsEmpty` + bound text; `N-pending-aborted` labelled add-arm and the five `N-strict-*` rows disclosed as one gate/two call sites in the harness docstring, TRACEABILITY, matrix and results; LOGBOOK REV3 lines. All KILLED 2/2 in my runs. |\n48|| Battery / tracecheck / digest / suite | REPRODUCED | 76-row battery: 75 KILLED + `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED, 2/2, harness exit 0 in every chunk, one raw log per plant per run (`mutants/producer-run{1,2}/`, `logs/producer-run{1,2}-chunk-*.log`); battery copy byte-identical to the candidate after both runs. `tracecheck` byte-equal to the quoted lines; `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted (`logs/section-*.log`). Digest re-derived by zeroing the pin in a throwaway copy → gate prints `4bd01143702d17bc05f187a14312cb868b85276b0f0b6d015c351929eae9bfc0` = pinned (`logs/digest-rederivation.log`). Package suite 95 PASS / 0 FAIL, 35 top-level tests (`logs/pkg-cloneproject-v.log`). |\n49|\n50|## Findings\n51|\n52|### P2 — raw-addressability is measured only at offset 0\n53|\n54|**P2-e Every raw-reference resolution in the committed suite targets a\n55|single-record member; no test witnesses a non-zero `offset`, so the\n56|natural offset-accumulation bug survives the whole suite while matrix\n57|row 4 reports \"Evidence ranges resolve to the exact captured bytes\n58|(manifest + descriptor linkage, in range)\" as driven.** `grep -n\n59|mustResolveRef *_test.go` finds seven call sites (`foreign_test.go:45,75,\n60|93,117`, `normalize_test.go:44,79,113`) — every one on a one-line member\n61|(line 1, offset 0) or on the whole-member opaque unit (offset 0 by\n62|construction). Plants run twice against `-run TestNormalize`\n63|(`reviewer-plants/run{1,2}/`, subprocess exit 0 both runs):\n64|\n65|| Plant | Edit (`native.go` / `dispatch.go`) | Verdict |\n66||---|---|---|\n67|| `RV-offset-drops-newline` | `offset += uint64(len(raw)) + 1` → `offset += uint64(len(raw))` (`splitRecordLines`; every record after line 1 references bytes shifted by its line index) | SURVIVED 2/2 |\n68|| `RV-offset-line-number` | `recordLine{... offset: offset + uint64(number) - 1 ...}` (line 1 exact, every later record off by its index) | SURVIVED 2/2 |\n69|| `RV-evidence-offset-second-line` | `evidenceFor`: exactly the line-2 record's `Offset` zeroed (its ref slices line 1's bytes) | SURVIVED 2/2 |\n70|| `RV-evidence-length-off-by-one` (control for the length axis) | `Length: record.Length - 1` for exactly the unprotected unknown-type record | KILLED 2/2 (5 tests) |\n71|\n72|Production is correct: on the pristine candidate a three-record member\n73|(`message/user` with multibyte text, unknown `frobnicate`, foreign\n74|`reasoning/encrypted`) projects offsets 0 / 142 / 285 with lengths equal to\n75|each line and every `RawRefs[0]` slices back to its own line byte-exact\n76|(`logs/probe-set2.log`, `TestReviewerProbeMultiRecordRefsResolve`). The\n77|finding is the measurement: the AC's \"keeps a Source Evidence whose raw\n78|blob/manifest byte-range references actually resolve back to the captured\n79|bytes\" is invariant (1)'s raw-addressability, the realistic member holds\n80|many records, and the suite proves the property only where `offset == 0`.\n81|The length axis IS pinned (the control kills), which is why this is a P2\n82|and not a P1: no shipped behaviour is wrong, one axis of an AC-named\n83|property is unmeasured and reported as measured.\n84|\n85|Ship: one committed row over a multi-record member that resolves EVERY\n86|event's `RawRefs[0]` against its own line and asserts the offsets\n87|(`0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2`) — the whole-member opaque unit and\n88|a CRLF-terminated line are useful extra records; a harness row for the\n89|offset-accumulation bug (labelled behaviour swap, like `N-overflow-truncate`,\n90|not a narrowing) that the new row kills; matrix row 4 and\n91|TRACEABILITY \"raw-addressable\" rows citing the multi-record test.\n92|\n93|### P3 — unpinned gates and prose (production correct in each case; each plant SURVIVED 2/2 against `-run TestNormalize`, `reviewer-plants/run{1,2}/`)\n94|\n95|- **P3-u optional-boolean null bound unstated.** `\"live_followup\":null`\n96|  and `\"live_attestation\":null` are admitted as `false`\n97|  (`bodyOptionalBool`: `json.Unmarshal(null, &bool)` leaves false;\n98|  `logs/probe-set2.log` PR2). `text:null`, `directives:null` and\n99|  `ciphertext:null` are stated; these two are not. State or refuse.\n100|- **P3-v body-level type and required-member gates carry no negative\n101|  row.** `body member %q is not a string` / `is not a boolean` /\n102|  `body misses member %q` refuse correctly on the pristine tree\n103|  (`\"text\":123`, `\"text\":{}`, `\"ciphertext\":123`, `\"call_id\":5`,\n104|  `\"live_attestation\":\"true\"`, `{}` — PR3 in `logs/probe-set2.log`) but no\n105|  committed test drives any of them: `RV-member-text-number` (the string\n106|  gate admits exactly the JSON number `123` for `text`) SURVIVED 2/2;\n107|  `RV-body-required-skip-text` (required check skipped for exactly `text`)\n108|  SURVIVED 2/2 — under that plant `{}` still refuses, with `is not a string`\n109|  instead of `misses member` (`logs/under-plant-RV-body-required-skip-text.log`),\n110|  so the required-member loop is a message-only gate. Add one row per gate\n111|  or state the message-only nature.\n112|- **P3-w empty-directive low edge unpinned.** `[\"\"]` and `[null]` refuse\n113|  `directive[0] is not a string[1..4096]` (PR4) but `RV-bound-directive-empty`\n114|  (`< 1` → `< 0`) SURVIVED 2/2; the stated per-edge bound names only the\n115|  upper edges (4096/4097). Name the low edge in the bound or add the row.\n116|  (`RV-bound-toolname-513` SURVIVED 2/2 inside the stated bound — listed for\n117|  the denominator only.)\n118|- **P3-x `doc.go:65` says \"the nine fixture-native known types\"** — there\n119|  are ten (`knownNativeType`, `native.go:231-242`); results and TRACEABILITY\n120|  say ten.\n121|- **P3-y refusal message shapes.** Actor-selector faults are wrapped twice\n122|  (`record store/session.jsonl line 1 cloneproject: invalid projection:\n123|  actor \"subagent:\" is outside ...`, PR12); the clonebundle parents-count\n124|  refusal names \"canonical session parents\" for event parents\n125|  (`logs/probe-clonebundle-bounds.log`, owner `internal/clonebundle`).\n126|  Cosmetic.\n127|- **P3-z `\"body\":null` on an unknown type is admitted** as an opaque\n128|  event (present-but-null satisfies the required-member rule; the body is\n129|  never read; PR16 in `logs/probe-set3.log`) while a missing body refuses.\n130|  Consistent with the \"unknown-type bodies are never read\" rule; say so in\n131|  the `unknown_type_without_body` bound text.\n132|- **P3-aa evidence archive hygiene.** `MANIFEST.sha256` lists itself (its\n133|  own line fails `shasum -c`); `cmds/cmd01-03.log` are empty with the exit\n134|  code recorded only in the results table. Cosmetic.\n135|\n136|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n137|\n138|1. **Invariant 1**: rows 1–5 reproduce; `N-unknown-kind`,\n139|   `N-unknown-kind-wholly`, `N-unknown-member` KILLED 2/2; a case-variant\n140|   type (`Message/User`) is simply unknown → `opaque_event`, never guessed;\n141|   an unknown type with a string, null or nested-duplicate body stays\n142|   opaque with the body never read (`logs/probe-set{2,3}.log`).\n143|2. **Invariant 2**: rows 6–10