{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d303","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b48a-1840-7d93-9d43-f2decee529f8"},"sequence":2012,"recorded_at":1780531400004019,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cc2eb299-8bb3-4a28-9487-6d4564236d15"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b494-81e0-7ed1-8afe-da3b10964571"},"task_id":"01a0b494-81e0-7ed1-8afe-da3b10964571","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b494-81e0-7ed1-8afe-da3b10964571","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/cloneproject/doc.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity\n4|// closure: Normalize derives a Canonical Session and Canonical Events\n5|// from captured bytes (a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed\n6|// Clone Raw Object Manifest, and the installed payload blobs). It is\n7|// the final leaf of the canonical-session-capture-and-evidence\n8|// story: contracts come from internal/clonebundle, capture from\n9|// internal/clonesnap, and this package owns normalization only.\n10|//\n11|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Sections\n12|// 7.8, 10.2, and 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md).\n13|//\n14|// The projection input is captured bytes, never hand-written\n15|// Canonical Events: every proof builds a fixture provider store,\n16|// runs clonesnap.Capture over it, and normalizes the sealed output.\n17|// Identical captured bytes produce byte-identical canonical output.\n18|//\n19|// Native records: the provider-native session log this package reads\n20|// is newline-delimited JSON (one record per line) carried by included\n21|// durable capture members. The envelope is fixture-native and NOT a\n22|// specification shape:\n23|//\n24|//\t{\"v\":1,\"native_event_id\":\"...\",\"native_type\":\"...\",\n25|//\t \"origin\":\"native|foreign\",\"protection\":\"none|encrypted|signed\",\n26|//\t \"actor\":\"main|subagent:<name>|external\",\"body\":{...}}\n27|//\n28|// Projection rules (each driven and mutated, see TRACEABILITY.md):\n29|//\n30|//   - Unknown native types become raw-addressable opaque_event\n31|//     records with opaque visibility, a whole-record byte-range\n32|//     reference, and reason unknown_native_event. Unknown-class\n33|//     members become one whole-member opaque_event. Nothing\n34|//     attributable is dropped, guessed, or re-typed.\n35|//   - Foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes opaque_reasoning\n36|//     with opaque visibility, preserved byte-exact through the blob\n37|//     store, never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated, or\n38|//     promoted. Foreign instructions are low-authority history: they\n39|//     never change the effective instruction snapshot.\n40|//   - Historical tools are inert. A tool_definition_snapshot never\n41|//     registers a callable tool (a captured live claim refuses).\n42|//     A tool_call resolves completed only with its tool_result;\n43|//     otherwise it becomes aborted history with reason\n44|//     unsafe_pending_action. Pending actions require a live work\n45|//     order, which capture never carries, so the live surface is\n46|//     always empty.\n47|//   - Source usage is counted into the source ledger only; target\n48|//     accounting stays zero.\n49|//   - Message-like text over 64 KiB becomes a Blob Descriptor\n50|//     reference to an installed overflow blob, never a truncation.\n51|//\n52|// Reuse, not fork: manifests, sessions, events, evidence, and the\n53|// unstable/maximal-safe gates come from internal/clonebundle;\n54|// overflow Blob Descriptors seal through clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor\n55|// and install through clonebundle.InstallRawBlob onto the landed\n56|// localstore no-replace discipline; digests and UUIDv7 come from\n57|// internal/scalar; strict JSON framing, character measures, and the\n58|// uint53 value gate come from internal/environ (DecodeStrictObject,\n59|// StringLength, CheckUint53Bounds). No rule is reimplemented where\n60|// a landed owner exists.\n61|//\n62|// Stated bounds (not waived): the fixture-native record envelope is\n63|// test-defined, not a specification shape; envelope extras are\n64|// unclaimed and can never override a claimed member (the envelope\n65|// is read from the strict map by exact name with no second\n66|// decoder); per-kind payload fact registries cover exactly the\n67|// facts this package emits for the nine fixture-native known types\n68|// (other Canonical kinds are never emitted here);\n69|// framing-malformed lines (unparseable JSON, lone surrogate\n70|// escapes, duplicate members, trailing data, missing envelope\n71|// members, contradictory protection claims, unknown body members)\n72|// refuse instead of projecting; every included non-unknown member\n73|// is parsed as the JSONL record log, so a non-JSONL member refuses\n74|// the whole projection (routing by member class is sibling scope);\n75|// per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge\n76|// (native_type, directives, call IDs, tool names) are deferred\n77|// (the shared StringLength gate is landed); \"directives\":null\n78|// decodes as zero directives and \"text\":null seals as empty inline\n79|// content; turn IDs and source timestamps are always null; tool\n80|// call arguments are not carried; unknown-class excluded members\n81|// project nothing (their bytes were never captured); 13.14.2-13.14.5\n82|// (fidelity dispositions, projection planning, transaction,\n83|// lineage) are sibling scope.","final_result":true}}}
