 bounds and NOT APPLICABLE (with owners)\n162|\n163|| Area | Status | Owner / evidence |\n164||---|---|---|\n165|| Fixture-native record envelope (`v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`, `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`) | Stated bound: test-defined framing, not a specification shape; body shapes exact; envelope extras unclaimed and unable to override a claimed member (strict-map read by exact name, no second decoder — pinned by `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers`) | this leaf (`doc.go`, `native.go` + refusal rows) |\n166|| Canonical kinds never emitted here (`session_started`, `approval_request`, `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`, `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`, `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) | NOT APPLICABLE: fact registries cover exactly the ten emitted kinds | normalization-sibling scope |\n167|| Non-text content blocks (`json`, `image`, `audio`, `document`, `resource_link`, `redacted`, `opaque`) | NOT APPLICABLE: this leaf seals `text` blocks only (inline or blob-referenced) | normalization-sibling scope; closed vocabulary enforced by the landed builder |\n168|| Capture statuses `partial`, `synthesized`, `unavailable` | NOT APPLICABLE: this leaf emits `exact` only | shape rules owned by the accepted `internal/clonebundle` suite |\n169|| Closed-shape internals (26-kind registry, 0..64 parents sorted-unique, UUIDv7, turn/time nullability, extensions, session scale bounds 1024/1M/1024) | Shape rules owned by the accepted `internal/clonebundle` suite; this leaf proves its output satisfies them by sealing + re-decoding every event and session (builder refusal = projection error) | `internal/clonebundle` (leaf 1, accepted) |\n170|| Actor UUIDv7 parsing | Gate owned by `internal/scalar`; entry refusal pinned by `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_actor_uuid` | `internal/scalar` (landed) |\n171|| `parent_actor_id` shape rule (null iff main) | Enforced by the landed builder; main-null asserted in `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape`, subagent-parent in `nested_subagent_call`, wiring narrowed by `N-main-parent` | `internal/clonebundle` builder + this leaf |\n172|| Closed core reason vocabulary (`unknown_native_event`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, `foreign_signature_unverifiable`, `unsafe_pending_action`, …) | Referenced, not owned: defined by §13.14.2; this leaf emits four codes as evidence strings without implementing dispositions | §13.14.2 owner (sibling) |\n173|| §13.14.2 fidelity dispositions, projection planning, lineage | NOT APPLICABLE: sibling scope | §13.14.2 owner (sibling) |\n174|| §13.14.3 Migration Checkpoint / bundle chain | NOT APPLICABLE: sibling scope | §13.14.3 owner (sibling) |\n175|| §13.14.4 transaction / staging | NOT APPLICABLE: this Story plans no projection, stages no target | §13.14.4 owner (sibling) |\n176|| §13.14.5 tuple admission | NOT APPLICABLE: this Story admits no tuple | §13.14.5 owner (sibling) |\n177|| §7.8 operation frames (capture-plan/capture/normalize) and the 8 MiB frame bound | NOT APPLICABLE here: owned and discharged by `sessadapter` (`session-adapter-frame-bound` case); this leaf owns the fidelity rules those operations must satisfy | `internal/sessadapter` (landed) |\n178|| Per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge (native_type 512/513, directive 4096/4097, call ID 512/513, tool names) | Stated bound: every edge checks through the landed `environ.StringLength` gate, but only the envelope ID edge carries a narrowing (`N-string-bound`) | this leaf (deferred rows) |\n179|| Non-JSONL included members | Stated bound, pinned: every included non-unknown member parses as the JSONL log; routing by member class is sibling scope | this leaf (`TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses`) |\n180|| `directives:null` | Stated bound, pinned: decodes as zero directives | this leaf (`TestNormalizeNullDirectivesDecodeAsEmpty`) |\n181|| `text:null` / `ciphertext:null` | Stated bound, pinned: null text seals as empty inline content (`TestNormalizeNullTextDecodesAsEmpty`); null ciphertext admitted but harmless (value never read) | this leaf |\n182|| Durable-write crash semantics (stage/fsync/verify/atomic install) | Owned by `internal/localstore` (landed fault suites); this leaf adds bundle atomicity (row 24) | `internal/localstore` (landed) |\n183|| `pending` live-work-order map parameter of `deriveLiveSurface` | Live-sibling API: `Normalize` always passes nil, so nothing captured can pend | live sibling (stated bound) |\n184|| Inherited advisories P3-a, P3-b, P3-c/d, P3-f, P3-g (capture-operation rows) | DEFERRED to a follow-up on `internal/clonesnap` (orchestrator-routed); this leaf changes no clonesnap behavior | clonesnap follow-up |\n185|| Inherited P3-e AfterWalk-seam bound | CLOSED here as a stated bound (`internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md` + results) | this leaf |\n186|| Inherited P3-η `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone contract | DEFERRED to a follow-up on the `internal/clonebundle` owner | clonebundle owner follow-up |\n187|| Inherited P3-ζ′ fidelity vocabulary spelled twice | BOUND: both spellings named with pinning tests; unification deferred to a follow-up on `internal/sessadapter` + `internal/clonesnap` | sessadapter/clonesnap follow-up |\n188|| Inherited P3-ζ lone surrogate | CLOSED here at the projection entry (rows 25–26 + narrowings) | this leaf |\n189|| `ax` command, `doctor` result, runtime capability | NOT CLAIMED anywhere in code, tests, README, or LOGBOOK | — |\n190|\n191|## E. Negative-evidence index\n192|\n193|Every refusal below is driven through `Normalize` over real captured bytes\n194|by the named committed test and reddened by the named narrowing (single\n195|member admitted). Production call sites: `Normalize` (`normalize.go`),\n196|`collectMembers` + `sealedEnvironment` (closure), `strictMembers` +\n197|`parseNativeLine` + `splitRecordLines` + body decoders (`native.go`),\n198|`dispatchRecord` / `dispatchProtected` (`dispatch.go`), `resolveToolCalls` +\n199|`deriveLiveSurface` (`tools.go`), `checkActors` + `buildEvents` +\n200|`buildResult` (`dispatch.go`).\n201|\n202|Refusal rows (46 in `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` + 3 standalone:\n203|`TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture`,\n204|`TestNormalizeRefusesEnvironmentDrift`,\n205|`TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses`): see section\n206|A rows 11, 13, 17, 23, 25–29, 31, 33–37, 39, 44 and section C. Token-preserving attacks:\n207|`N-native-type-token` (the `message/user` label still matches, routes to\n208|`assistant_message`; killer `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` executes the\n209|behavioral suite) and `N-protection-encrypted` (the `encrypted` label still\n210|matches, skips opaque dispatch; killer `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque`).\n211|The six `N-alias-*` rows restore the case-folded read for exactly one\n212|envelope member each (killers: the six axis subtests of\n213|`TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers`).\n214|Labelled non-narrowings: `N-empty-projection` (single-member class),\n215|`N-overflow-truncate` (behaviour swap), and `N-pending-aborted`\n216|(add-arm: `Normalize` passes nil live work orders).\n217|Harmless control: `C-doc-comment` (comment-only edit, SURVIVED exit 0 both\n218|runs), proving the harness observes outcomes instead of hard-coding kills.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
